10
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
The Zookeeper's Wife is a 2017 war drama film directed by Niki Caro,
based on the 2007 non-fiction book by Diane Ackerman.

11
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
The film tells the story of how Jan and Antonina Żabiński rescued hundreds of Polish Jews
from the Germans by hiding them in their Warsaw zoo during World War II.

12
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
It stars Jessica Chastain, Johan Heldenbergh,
Daniel Brühl and Michael McElhatton.

13
01:31:00,000 --> 01:31:06,000
The Zookeeper's Wife had its world premiere on 8 March 2017 in Warsaw, Poland, the location of the story,
followed by its US premiere at the Cinequest Film Festival in San Jose, California, on 12 March 2017.

14
01:38:00,000 --> 01:38:06,000
It was released in the United States on 31 March and in
the United Kingdom on 21 April 2017.

15
01:45:00,000 --> 01:45:06,000
The film received mixed reviews from critics, and
grossed $26 million on a $20 million budget.

16
01:52:00,000 --> 01:52:06,000
The film explores themes of nazi, holocaust (shoah), world
war ii, biography, based on true story.

17
01:59:00,000 --> 01:59:06,000
The tone is emotional.
